{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Screaming Resonance Lead",
 "category": "Leads and stabs",
 "text": "Sound: a piercing, whistling, almost feedback-like lead: a filter on the edge of singing by itself, swelling into each note and screaming through distortion and echoes.\n\nHow it's built: a saw into the Ladder filter with RESONANCE almost at the top, so the filter rings a strong pitch of its own; KEY follows the notes so the ring stays in tune; an envelope with a slow ATTACK opens the CUTOFF so each note swells into the scream. Drive, a long Delay, a Reverb. One voice.\n\nPlay: slow, held notes and bends.\n\nTweak: RESONANCE (careful near the top), the filter envelope's ATTACK, DRIVE, the delay's FEEDBACK.",
